From 0e5b0d59d14c961541c033ff3e6371739598b7e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:29:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] wip-kv-residency: A2 -- mixed-backing windowed KV (one VA
 range, host tail + VRAM window)

TODO #118 Goal A, slice A2.  The KV cache keeps ONE tensor in ONE VA reservation; the cells below the
window are backed by PINNED SYSTEM RAM and the rest by VRAM.  No kernel change, no op change, and every
cell-walking path (the set_rows writers, the in-place rope shift behind defrag/seq_add, state
save/restore, clear, the kq mask) keeps addressing one contiguous range -- which is why this route was
chosen over A1's two-base read (kept on branch wip-kv-residency-a1-two-base).

  ggml-cuda-vmm-region: the mapped extent is a mapping TABLE ((off, bytes, kind)) instead of a per-unit
    bitmap, because mixed backing needs a 2 MiB bulk and a 4 KiB-granular segment boundary in the same
    reservation.  map_span(off, bytes, host) rounds outwards to the driver's MINIMUM granularity (4 KiB)
    and never overlaps.  The selftest now also maps a HOST-backed span, has the device write it, and
    reads it back.
  ggml-cuda.cu: ggml_backend_cuda_kv_region_buffer_type_split(device, tail_bytes) -- one buft instance
    per split.  grow_cells maps host [0, tail) and device [tail, cells) as the CELL WATERMARK advances,
    so a short run pins only the tail it reaches; grow_for decides the kind by position for the
    arbitrary-index writes (state restore).  The one INFO line reports system-RAM vs VRAM bytes.
  llama-kv-cache.cpp: the split point (LLAMA_KV_RESIDENT_CELLS=W, LLAMA_KV_REGION=1 to enable the
    provider) with a loud always-printed warning; it DECLINES (no spill) when the K/V cell geometry is
    not uniform across layers.  Decided at creation, before SLAB_INIT.

Measured (1 GPU, gfx1201):
  * text byte-identical off / region-only / window 2048 / 4096 on 4B and 27B (q8_0) and on 35B-A3B
    -ncmoe 24; prefill logits KLD 0.000000 / 100.000 %; no GPU faults;
  * the Goal A OOM config now RUNS: 27B Q8_0 -c 262144 q8_0, 8704 MiB KV = 8160 MiB system RAM +
    544 MiB VRAM, prefill 933 t/s;
  * at 51 475 tokens of depth: 18.7 t/s fully resident, 13.6 t/s with a 32 768-cell window (636 MiB of
    spill per token), 10.8 t/s with a 16 384-cell window (1.19 GiB) -- the measured cost matches
    (used - resident) x cell_bytes / ~28 GB/s;
  * slab mode: 35B-A3B -ncmoe 24 -c 262144, SLAB_INIT free 19.80 -> 22.46 GiB, slab mapped
    18.75 -> 21.44 GiB, i.e. the arena gains the 2.69 GiB the window frees (decode flat).

FINDING (recorded in wip/kv-residency/MIXED-BACKING.md): a static window anchored at the END of -c only
helps once the run reaches it -- at 51k tokens in a -c 262144 cache the whole used extent is still in the
tail.  The product knob has to follow the watermark (a sliding window: unmap/remap one chunk as it
advances, which the probe's T7 showed is a few us), not sit at the end of the context.

Not for patches/: nothing here is in the delivery set.
